# Judges' lab settings (ADR-0013, ADR-0026).
# A variable already set in the environment is kept. Secrets do not go here:
# they go in lab/.env, which is not committed. See lab/.env.example.
#
# Third-party image tags below were not pulled when this file was written.
# The seat had no DNS, and docker was denied. The first `make up` is the check.

COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=proven-lab

GOLANG_IMAGE=golang:1.26.10
RUNTIME_IMAGE=alpine:3.23

PROVEN_REGISTRY=docker.io
PROVEN_IMAGE=saphan/proven
PUSH_PLATFORMS=linux/amd64,linux/arm64

SCOUT_REFUSE_SEVERITIES=critical,high

GITEA_VERSION=1.22.6
GITEA_HTTP_PORT=3300
# Not published. The lab does not serve SSH. See GITEA_DISABLE_SSH.
GITEA_SSH_PORT=2222
# The image already runs OpenSSH on :22. Gitea's own server on that port
# exited the container (measured 2026-10-23, make up). The lab needs no SSH.
GITEA_DISABLE_SSH=true
GITEA_START_SSH_SERVER=false
GITEA_CONTAINER_HTTP_PORT=3000
GITEA_INTERNAL_HOST=gitea
# Account for every `gitea` command. The image refuses that command as root,
# and `compose exec` is root when no user is named (measured 2026-10-23).
GITEA_RUN_USER=git
DIND_HOST=dind
DIND_PORT=2375

# Grafana's OpenTelemetry stack in one image: collector, Prometheus, Tempo, Loki
# and Grafana (ADR-0045). It runs as its own container and is not part of
# Proven's image. The tag below was not pulled when this file was written (the
# seat had no DNS and no docker); the first `make up` is the check.
LGTM_IMAGE=grafana/otel-lgtm
LGTM_VERSION=0.11.0
LGTM_INTERNAL_HOST=lgtm
# Grafana: the port the lab publishes on 127.0.0.1, and the port the image serves it on.
LGTM_GRAFANA_PORT=3301
LGTM_GRAFANA_CONTAINER_PORT=3000
# The collector's OTLP/HTTP port: published on 127.0.0.1 so a review run on the
# host can be exported too, and the port the image serves it on.
LGTM_OTLP_PORT=4318
LGTM_OTLP_CONTAINER_PORT=4318
# The dashboard's uid, from lab/grafana/dashboards/proven-review.json.
LGTM_DASHBOARD_UID=proven-review
# What the lab's pull-request review is told (the standard OTEL_* names).
# A short interval, so the dashboard moves while the review runs.
LAB_OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=proven
# The second reviewer model of the lab's review (proven.yaml: special_reviewer),
# so the dashboard has two reviewers to show side by side. Empty: one reviewer.
LAB_SPECIAL_REVIEWER=qwen
LAB_OTEL_METRIC_EXPORT_INTERVAL=1000
# How long `make up` waits for Grafana, and `make trace` for the review's trace, in seconds.
LGTM_WAIT_SECONDS=120
TRACE_WAIT_SECONDS=90

ACT_RUNNER_VERSION=0.2.11
DOCKER_VERSION=29.9.1

# The image the Prover runs each test in, and the digest `make up` pulls it by.
# PROVEN_TEST_IMAGE is the setting the Prover reads. Its default is the same.
# TEST_IMAGE_DIGEST pins the pull: it is the digest of the golang:1.26 index
# (both platforms), read from Docker Hub on 2026-10-23. Empty, `make up` pulls
# the tag and prints the digest it got.
PROVEN_TEST_IMAGE=golang:1.26
TEST_IMAGE_DIGEST=sha256:672c944cfd07599b5f1bb179869270cdc94c6254e41db4d431259693cb286b82

# The lab's start page: one static page, served by a small nginx on 127.0.0.1, at LAB_PAGE_PATH.
# up.sh renders it from lab/page/lab.html.tmpl into the lab's page volume. The image runs as a
# user that is not root and listens on LAB_PAGE_CONTAINER_PORT. LAB_PAGE_PATH is also written in
# lab/page/nginx.conf; a test holds the two together. The tag was not pulled when this file was
# written (no network on the seat); the first `make up` is the check.
#
# The page carries the lab's password. Its port line in lab/compose.yaml names 127.0.0.1, like every other port, and
# no setting moves it. A LAB_PAGE_BIND in the environment that is not loopback is refused by name before anything
# starts (lab_require_loopback in lab/scripts/lib.sh); there is no such setting here.
LAB_PAGE_PORT=3302
LAB_PAGE_PATH=/lab
LAB_PAGE_IMAGE=nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged
LAB_PAGE_IMAGE_VERSION=1.27-alpine
LAB_PAGE_CONTAINER_PORT=8080

# Proven's documentation site (docs-site/Dockerfile) as a lab service, on 127.0.0.1.
# The image is built by `make up`; a build that fails is named and the lab goes on.
LAB_DOCS_PORT=3303
LAB_DOCS_CONTAINER_PORT=3000
DOCS_IMAGE=saphan/proven-docs
DOCS_IMAGE_TAG=1
NODE_IMAGE=node:22-alpine

RUNNER_NAME=proven-lab
RUNNER_LABEL=ubuntu-latest

LAB_ADMIN_USER=proven
LAB_ADMIN_EMAIL=proven@localhost
LAB_BOT_USER=proven-bot
LAB_BOT_EMAIL=proven-bot@lab.local
LAB_DEMO_REPO=discount
LAB_DEMO_BASE=main
# The branch of the first demo pull request (lab/seed/prs.tsv, the logic-bug change).
LAB_DEMO_HEAD=demo-discount

SEED_IMAGE=saphan/proven-lab-seed
SEED_IMAGE_TAG=2

# --- Going live (ADR-0052, docs/LAB.md "Go live") ---
# `make up` reads lab/.env when it exists and stores each NON-EMPTY setting named here as an Actions secret of the
# demo repository. An empty one is removed from the repository, so deleting a key from lab/.env returns the lab to
# sample mode. The values are never written to a file, an image or a log. The workflow runs a live review when a
# generator key, a Nightshift token or the gateway pair is stored, and a sample review otherwise.
LAB_LIVE_KEYS=PROVEN_GENERATOR_MODE PROVEN_GENERATOR_KEY PROVEN_NVIDIA_BASE_URL PROVEN_GUARDRAIL_MODE PROVEN_GUARDRAIL_KEY PROVEN_GENERATOR_BASE_URL METERLESS_RUNTIME_TOKEN ZETARIS_REST_URL ZETARIS_API_KEY ZETARIS_ORG_ID PROVEN_GENERATOR_MODEL PROVEN_GENERATOR_REQUIRE_NVIDIA JUDGES_GATEWAY_URL JUDGES_GATEWAY_TOKEN JUDGES_GATEWAY_ACCESS_TOKEN PROVEN_MARKOVIAN PROVEN_LAB_SCOUT_INTENT
# The Meterless features among them: settings of a review, not keys. They are stored the same way, keep sample mode
# and do not make the lab live (lab/scripts/flow.sh, lab/seed/golive.sh).
LAB_FEATURE_KEYS=PROVEN_MARKOVIAN PROVEN_LAB_SCOUT_INTENT
# The credentials among them, ruled secret by what each opens: a generator key, a guardrail key, the Nightshift runtime
# token, the Zetaris key, and the judge's two gateway credentials. They travel to the seed as the 0600 file /state/secrets,
# written over stdin by make up (lab_write_secrets in lab/scripts/lib.sh), and are named nowhere in lab/compose.yaml. The
# other names of LAB_LIVE_KEYS (modes, URLs, model names, the organisation id, the feature switches) open nothing.
LAB_SECRET_KEYS=PROVEN_GENERATOR_KEY PROVEN_GUARDRAIL_KEY METERLESS_RUNTIME_TOKEN ZETARIS_API_KEY JUDGES_GATEWAY_TOKEN JUDGES_GATEWAY_ACCESS_TOKEN
# Path B, the judges' gateway. The gateway's address and the judge's token are the two secrets above. W18 builds the
# gateway; these names are this lab's, chosen because W18's order was not on this branch. Where the gateway serves
# Zetaris, relative to JUDGES_GATEWAY_URL, and the organisation id the gateway expects in front of Zetaris.
JUDGES_GATEWAY_ZETARIS_PATH=/zetaris/api/v1.0
JUDGES_GATEWAY_ZETARIS_ORG_ID=0
# The start-up flow's one check of the gateway (lab/scripts/flow.sh): a POST of an empty JSON object to this path.
# It is the evidence route, which accepts only a Proven query-template request, so it spends nothing: credentials the
# gateway accepts get 400 not_a_template_request, refused ones 401 or 403. Seconds to wait for the answer.
# (Claim to test with W18: the evidence route is where the Zetaris path above is served.)
JUDGES_GATEWAY_CHECK_SECONDS=20

# The start-up flow's answers (flow.sh) have settings of their own, read from the environment and from lab/.env, so a
# script never waits at a question: PROVEN_LAB_MODE=sample|live, PROVEN_LAB_JUDGE=yes|no, PROVEN_LAB_BACKEND=ours|own,
# PROVEN_LAB_GATEWAY_AUTH=access|token (default access), PROVEN_LAB_OWN_SETUP=yes|no, PROVEN_LAB_USE_DETECTED=yes|no.
# They are not set here: an unset one is asked on a terminal, and means sample with no terminal.
# Your own setup, what the organisers' guide installs: Zetaris's REST service (localhost:8888) and Nightshift's
# runtime (127.0.0.1:8088). The flow asks them one request each, and offers to use what answers.
DETECT_ZETARIS_URL=http://localhost:8888/api/v1.0
DETECT_NIGHTSHIFT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8088/v1/models
# How the lab's review job, which runs inside the lab's own Docker, names this machine.
LAB_JOB_HOST_ALIAS=host.docker.internal

# Path C, Zetaris on this machine (`make up ZETARIS=local`). Empty ZETARIS: not started.
# The sponsor's platform is a bundle the judge downloads from their own Zetaris account, and its images are in the
# sponsor's registry behind the judge's own sign-in. ZETARIS_COMPOSE_FILE is the bundle's docker-compose.yml.
ZETARIS=
ZETARIS_COMPOSE_FILE=
ZETARIS_PROJECT=proven-zetaris
ZETARIS_API_PORT=8888
ZETARIS_REST_PATH=/api/v1.0
ZETARIS_LAB_ALIAS=zetaris-api
# The loopback ports the platform's console and REST service are published on (never another address).
ZETARIS_WAIT_SECONDS=180
ZETARIS_UI_HOST_PORT=3304
ZETARIS_API_HOST_PORT=8888
# Path C, Nightshift in a Tart VM (`make nightshift`, macOS on Apple silicon only).
NIGHTSHIFT_VM_SCRIPT=hackathon/fleet/infra/nightshift-vm/nightshift_vm.sh
NIGHTSHIFT_VM_NAME=nightshift
NIGHTSHIFT_PORT=8088
NIGHTSHIFT_HEALTH_PATH=/v1/models
NIGHTSHIFT_WAIT_SECONDS=300

# The sample review runs every agent, both reviewers and the fixer; on a small lab host it takes more than three
# minutes (measured 2026-10-25), so e2e waits up to fifteen (seven pull requests are reviewed, three at a time).
E2E_WAIT_SECONDS=900
E2E_POLL_SECONDS=5
